---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const { company, privacy } = site;
const lastUpdated = new Date(`${privacy.lastUpdated}T00:00:00Z`);
const lastUpdatedLabel = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
	day: 'numeric',
	month: 'long',
	year: 'numeric',
	timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(lastUpdated);
---

<Layout
	title={`Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`}
	description={`How ${site.name} processes personal data when you visit this website or contact us.`}
>
	<SiteHeader />

	<main id="main">
		<section class="section legal">
			<div class="container">
				<div class="legal-inner">
					<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
					<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
					<p class="lead">
						This policy describes what personal data is processed when you visit this website or
						contact us, on what legal basis, for how long, and what rights you have.
					</p>

					<dl class="legal-meta">
						<div>
							<dt>Controller</dt>
							<dd>{company.legalName}</dd>
						</div>
						<div>
							<dt>Company ID (IČO)</dt>
							<dd>{company.companyId}</dd>
						</div>
						<div>
							<dt>Registered seat</dt>
							<dd>
								{company.street}, {company.district}, {company.postalCode} {company.city}, {company.country}
							</dd>
						</div>
						<div>
							<dt>Contact</dt>
							<dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd>
						</div>
					</dl>

					<div class="legal-body">
						<h2>1. What data is processed and why</h2>

						<h3>Web hosting</h3>
						<p>
							The site is hosted by an external hosting provider. Each page load necessarily
							generates operational data — in particular IP address, browser type and version,
							access time and requested URL. These data serve solely for the technical operation
							and security of the service; the controller does not access them in a form that
							would allow tracking individual visitors. The controller does not control the
							hosting provider's internal data handling and does not guarantee its practices;
							these are governed by the provider's own terms and privacy policy. Details of the
							provider are available on request.
						</p>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>Legal basis:</strong> legitimate interest in the technical operation and
								security of the service (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Third-country transfer:</strong> the hosting provider processes operational
								data in the United States. Transfers rely on safeguards such as the EU–US Data
								Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. Details are available on
								request.
							</li>
						</ul>

						<h3>Contacting us (e-mail)</h3>
						<p>
							If you write us an e-mail or use another contact channel listed on the site, we
							process the data you provide in that contact — in particular your e-mail address,
							name and the message content.
						</p>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>Legal basis:</strong> steps prior to entering into a contract at your
								request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR), or legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) for
								answering enquiries.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Purpose:</strong> handling your enquiry and any related follow-up
								communication.
							</li>
						</ul>

						<h2>2. Cookies and active analytics</h2>
						<p>
							This website does not set cookies for analytics, advertising or tracking, and does
							not use fingerprinting or any other technology aimed at identifying users or their
							devices. We do not run active web analytics, so visits cannot be tracked or
							profiled.
						</p>
						<p>
							The contact section embeds a map from OpenStreetMap. Loading the map transmits your
							IP address and browser information to the OpenStreetMap Foundation so the map can be
							displayed; its privacy policy applies.
						</p>
						<p>
							Other than the OpenStreetMap embed, the site loads no third-party scripts or fonts
							from external servers.
						</p>
						{/* TODO: when the cookie consent tool is added, describe the consent choice stored in the browser and link to "Cookie settings". */}

						<h2>3. Data retention</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>Hosting operational data:</strong> retained by the hosting provider
								according to its terms and internal policies (typically only as long as necessary
								for operation and security).
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Correspondence from the contact channel:</strong> for the duration of
								handling your enquiry and thereafter only as necessary; max. {privacy.retentionPeriod}.
							</li>
						</ul>

						<h2>4. Your rights</h2>
						<p>
							You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing,
							portability, and the right to object to processing based on legitimate interest.
							Exercise them at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
						</p>
						<p>
							You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority — the
							Czech Office for Personal Data Protection (Úřad pro ochranu osobních údajů), Pplk.
							Sochora 27, 170 00 Prague 7,
							<a href="https://www.uoou.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.uoou.cz</a>.
						</p>

						<h2>5. Security</h2>
						<p>
							The site is static and processes no data on its own server side. Communication is
							encrypted (HTTPS). Data from contact channels is stored in our e-mail systems,
							accessible only to authorised personnel.
						</p>

						<h2>6. Changes to this policy</h2>
						<p>
							We may update this policy; the version published on this page is always the current
							one.
						</p>
					</div>

					<p class="legal-updated">
						Last updated: <time datetime={privacy.lastUpdated}>{lastUpdatedLabel}</time>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</Layout>
